  "body": "## What changed\n\nIn `iso.rs` `tet`, a marching-tetrahedra crossing is put on a sample when that sample's field value is under `NODE_SNAP` (1e-6) of the value span along the edge (`|da| < NODE_SNAP * |da - db|`, and the same for `db`).\n\nA cut floor on the extraction lattice leaves field values of about 1e-12 at the samples. The crossing then sat about 1e-12 mm from the sample, under the 1e-9 weld that `open_edges` uses. `push` kept the facets that shared it, and they collapsed after a weld or an f32 export. With the snap, those facets are exactly zero-area, and `push` already drops them. At a 0.25 mm step the snap moves a corner at most 0.43 nm (a body diagonal of the cell). The test reads `|da|`, `|db|` and `|da - db|`, which are the same numbers when the edge is crossed from its other end, so the two tetrahedra that share an edge snap together or not at all. A snapped corner is the sample itself, not `pa + (pb - pa)`, which beside a coordinate's rounding residue is not always `pb`.\n\nDual contouring is not changed. Neither is `open_edges`: the issue also proposed making it count every edge, but several tests use it as their closed-mesh check, so that is left for a separate change if wanted (see the decision file). The new pins count every edge themselves.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe issue's synthetic block (30 x 30 x 20 mm at cell 0.5, four passes of a flat tool of radius 3), meshed with `IsoMethod::Marching`, then welded on the 1e-9 lattice:\n\n| Floor height | Before: collapsed facets / edges not on two facets | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| 15.25 (on the lattice) | 11,394 / 5,799 | 0 / 0 |\n| 15.1 (off the lattice) | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nSynthetic shapes only. Two tests join the existing `stock_dual` suite (`crates/sim/tests/stock_dual.rs`, whose gate map already covers `stock_sim::iso`), so no new test binary:\n- `a_floor_on_the_lattice_meshes_to_a_valid_solid_by_marching_tetrahedra`: fails on the old code with (11,394, 5,799).\n- `a_floor_off_the_lattice_stays_valid_by_both_methods`: Marching and Dual.\n\nTwo unit tests in `iso.rs`:\n- `an_edge_gets_the_same_corner_from_either_end_at_the_snap_threshold`: crosses one edge from each end at 8,000 values around the threshold. It fails on a first form of this fix that tested the fraction `t` (one value snapped from one end and not the other, 1e-6 of an edge apart) and passes now.\n- `a_snapped_corner_is_the_sample_itself`: 20,000 tetrahedra with a zero-valued sample beside a rounding residue; it fails when the snapped corner is computed as `pa + (pb - pa)` and passes now.\n\n`stock_export` and the sim unit tests pass.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head `1cce59a57` (upstream/main `a1c57b4` merged in, review fixes in `503d97b3e` and `1cce59a57`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 4 steps (sim build, sim lib, `stock_dual`, `stock_export`), 0 failed, 0 stalled, 5.7 min.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nOn the first head `6a11bbc7f` (base `f8748d97d`, before the review fixes; the later merges touched none of the changed files):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 5 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 9.9 min.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: green, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 83.2 min (most of it the release build, on a shared box).\n\n- No heavy step: this is not a `P1` (work-issue section 3).\n\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/4107-marching-node-snap.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes.\n- The GUI.\n- The mesh volume is not pinned. A corner moves at most 1e-6 of a lattice edge.\n- A crossing between 1e-6 of an edge and the f32 rounding step from a sample can still collapse after an f32 export. That is general marching behaviour, not this floor case.\n\nEffort: high (stock simulation is under the safety floor).\nChangelog: Stock simulation: a cut floor on the extraction lattice now meshes to a valid solid by marching tetrahedra; before, picometre slivers collapsed after a weld or an f32 export and left edges on three or more facets.\n\nBranch: upstream/main merged in (plain merge); the diff is 3 files: `iso.rs`, `stock_dual.rs` and the decision file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4107\n",
